{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2094082456/17/codegen_prompts/4.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/17`\n- 题号：`4`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2094082456/17/4.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"4\">\n- `description`：利用网格边缘的颜色序列条作为\"绘图指令\"，在中央画布上逐步绘制嵌套的彩色矩形环。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格的最左列是一个自上而下排列的颜色序列条，由若干种不同颜色的像素组成（每种颜色占连续若干个像素）。该列中不含黑色像素。\n  - 网格的最上行（不含第一列的交叉像素）是另一个自左而右排列的颜色序列条，同样由若干种不同颜色的像素组成，每种颜色占连续若干个像素，不含黑色。\n  - 网格其余区域（不含最左列和最上行）为全黑的\"画布\"区域。\n  - 最左列中每段连续同色像素的长度记录了对应矩形环在垂直方向上的厚度；最上行中每段连续同色像素的长度记录了对应矩形环在水平方向上的厚度。\n  - 最左列与最上行的颜色段数量相同，且颜色按顺序一一对应（第一段对应第一段，依此类推），定义同一个矩形环的颜色。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 从最外层开始，依次绘制嵌套矩形环：第一个颜色段定义最外层环，第二个颜色段定义次外层环，依此类推。\n  - 每个矩形环的上下厚度等于最左列对应颜色段的像素数，左右厚度等于最上行对应颜色段的像素数。\n  - 矩形环从画布区域的外边界开始向内嵌套绘制：第一个环紧贴画布边界，第二个环紧贴第一个环的内边界，以此类推。\n  - 每个环的颜色为对应颜色段的颜色。\n  - 最左列和最上行在输出中保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：边缘的两个颜色序列条不是简单的图例，而是分别编码了矩形环在两个维度上的厚度——解题者需要发现\"颜色段长度 = 环厚度\"这一数值编码关系，并且需要理解两条序列如何协同定义非正方形的矩形环。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/ac6f9922, train/42f83767, eval/88e364bc, train/d749d46f, eval/3e6067c3, eval/58490d8a, eval/332f06d7, eval/dbff022c\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ac6f9922\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3159\nmechanism=0.4021\nlexical=0.0123\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/ac6f9922.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ac6f9922.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSummarize the enclosed table slots by the single object color inside each slot, using the slot background color for empty slots.\n\nInput structure\n- The most common color forms the outer background and all enclosed slot\n  backgrounds.\n- The enclosed background components form a complete rectangular array of\n  slots, ordered by their positions.\n- Each slot contains either no other color or exactly one object color.\n\nRule\n- Find all 4-connected components of the most common color that do not touch\n  the input edge.\n- Sort their bounding boxes into row and column order to define the output\n  table.\n- For each slot, output its unique non-background color if present; otherwise\n  output the background color.\n\nKey insight\n- The large grid is an expanded table: the enclosed background components are\n  the cells, and any colored object drawn inside a cell is that cell's summary\n  value.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"enclosed 4-connected background-color slot components arranged as a rectangular table, each containing zero or one non-background object color\",\n  \"transform\": \"collapse each slot to one output pixel in row/column order: use the contained object color if present, otherwise use the background color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"number of slot rows x number of slot columns\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"42f83767\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2991\nmechanism=0.3773\nlexical=0.0127\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:square, object:template, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/42f83767.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/42f83767.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExpand the lower color grid by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.\n\nInput structure\nThe input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.\nThe legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,\nthe same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.\n\nRule\nPair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in\nthe lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,\nrecoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.\n\nKey insight\nThe lower grid is not copied directly; it is an index grid whose colors select\nthe stencil shape from the legend, so each input pixel becomes one square block.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"legend stencil s paired with color swatch s.color\",\n  \"dst\": \"output block d for a lower-grid pixel\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.input_pixel_color\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor s.mask with d.input_pixel_color; stencil holes remain background\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"lower grid height and width multiplied by stencil size\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3109\nmechanism=0.3875\nlexical=0.0122\ncode_feature=0.3750\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, object:template, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\nRule:\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\n\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Yellow pixels inside colored-border regions move in the direction indicated by the red pixel in the legend with matching background color, stopping at region boundary.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"yellow pixels inside colored-border regions s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"move(s, direction=legend.red_pixel_offset) where legend.background_color == s.containing_region.border_color until s.touches(region_boundary)\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend on grid edge with background color C and red pixel indicates: yellow pixels in regions with border color C move in direction from blue center to red pixel\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"legend/control-pixels\",\n    \"region-membership\",\n    \"directional-movement\",\n    \"boundary-collision\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d749d46f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3072\nmechanism=0.3893\nlexical=0.0124\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/d749d46f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPack each solid foreground rectangle twice: wide across the top and tall from the bottom.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one background color and one foreground color; the foreground forms\nseparate solid rectangles, ordered from left to right.\n\nRule\nBuild a 10-row background canvas whose width is the packed width of the wide\nversions of the rectangles. For each source rectangle, paint a top-aligned\nrectangle of shape min(h,w) by max(h,w), with one background column between\nconsecutive rectangles. Then, starting again from the left edge, paint a\nbottom-aligned rectangle of shape max(h,w) by min(h,w) for each source rectangle,\nagain separated by one background column.\n\nKey insight\nThe input rectangles are not copied in their original orientations; each object\ncontributes one horizontal-facing and one vertical-facing normalized rectangle,\npreserving left-to-right object order.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"solid monochromatic foreground rectangles ordered left-to-right\",\n  \"dst\": \"packed upper wide slots and lower tall slots in the same left-to-right order\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"rank(s) == rank(d) for both the upper and lower slot sequences\",\n  \"transform\": \"paint each rectangle twice: min(h,w) by max(h,w) top-aligned in the upper band, and max(h,w) by min(h,w) bottom-aligned in the lower band, with one background column between slots\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"height 10; width is the sum of max(h,w) over source rectangles plus one separator column between consecutive rectangles\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"3e6067c3\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2768\nmechanism=0.2857\nlexical=0.0124\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:square, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/3e6067c3.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3e6067c3.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nConnect framed squares via colored bridges following a control-pixel sequence.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. Border color forms equal-sized framed squares with unique inner fill colors.\n- Control row below squares: colored pixels read left-to-right encode visitation order.\n\nRule:\n- Start at the square matching first control color c0.\n- For each consecutive pair (ci, ci+1), find the ci+1-colored square aligned in the same row or column band, preferring nearest.\n- Draw a bridge colored ci between the pair, spanning the gap with inner-square thickness.\n\nKey insight: Row/column-band alignment plus proximity resolves ambiguity when inner colors repeat.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"adjacent pixel pair s in a sequence of control pixels in bottom area\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"keep src\",\n  \"dst\": \"merge with adjacent square pair d in an array of squares with colored inner square in main area\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.colors == d.inner_squares.colors\",\n  \"transform\": \"connect d.inner_squares with s[0].color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"process control pairs from left to right\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"control pixels indicates connection path\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"58490d8a\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3132\nmechanism=0.4056\nlexical=0.0155\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:rectangle, object:template, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
